Description: skip style.css symlink generation when manual is absent (nodoc)
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-05-17
Bug-Athena: debian/p7zip-full.links is an executable config script that
 generates symlinks deduplicating style.css across the HTML manual
 subdirs under /usr/share/doc/p7zip-full/DOC/MANUAL/.  Under
 DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nodoc the manual isn't installed, so $maindir
 doesn't exist and the script exits with "does not exist" error 1.
 .
 dh_link then fails with "executable config returned exit code 1"
 and the whole build dies.  Fix: when the manual isn't present
 (legitimate nodoc build), exit 0 with no symlinks to generate.
 .
 Behaviour with manual present (default upstream build) is unchanged.
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/p7zip-full.links
+++ b/debian/p7zip-full.links
@@ -12,7 +12,11 @@ readonly maindir="usr/share/doc/$pkg/DOC/MANUAL"

 unset CDPATH
 cd debian/$pkg >/dev/null
-[ -e "$maindir/$file" ]   || { echo "$maindir/$file does not exist" >&2; exit 1; }
+# Athena fork — under DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nodoc the manual isn't installed,
+# so $maindir is absent and there's nothing to symlink.  Exit cleanly
+# instead of failing dh_link.  Behaviour with the manual present is
+# unchanged (the loop below produces the dedupe links as before).
+[ -e "$maindir/$file" ]   || { echo "$maindir/$file absent (nodoc build?), no symlinks needed" >&2; exit 0; }

 for dir in $(find "$maindir" -mindepth 1 -type d -print); do
   set -- "$maindir/$file" "$dir/$file"
